# OPEN PROBLEMS

**Updated:** 2026-09-28

## O1 — Persistent conditioned factor histograms for GF(2)-rank r

Given `M=UV` over GF(2), characterize the minimal exact persistent state supporting all coordinate-conditioned counts of order <=k. Establish storage and query complexity in `(p,q,r,k)` and determine gauge-invariant formulations.

## O2 — Lower bounds for rank-r persistent summaries

Does exact support for all bounded coordinate restrictions force `Omega(2^r)` state information in the worst case? Can a communication/linear-sketch argument prove optimality of a factor-state histogram representation?

## O3 — Complete kappa landscape for natural representation classes

Determine exact or asymptotic `kappa(C)` for:
- read-once formulas;
- OBDD/ROBDD of bounded width;
- d-DNNF / SDD under natural size/width parameters;
- Kronecker/product-structured truth tensors;
- bounded cofactor-prototype classes;
- tensor trains of bounded rank.

## O4 — Does the parity obstruction cross all four artifact families?

The obstruction is proved for GF(2)-rank <=2 and for classes containing affine/ANF functions. Verify the exact definitions of the disjoint-XOR, cofactor/prototype, and Kronecker families from the structural-computation manuscript and determine whether each contains a size-poly(n) representation of the global parity pair. If yes, their worst-case reconstruction threshold is n despite compact representation.

## O5 — Nonlinear compression of Q_k fibers

For Boolean functions, characterize the number and geometry of realizable low-order marginal vectors and derive bit-complexity lower/upper bounds for exact summaries, beyond the ambient linear dimension `sum_{j<=k} C(n,j)`.

## O6 — Minimal-collision classification in query language

Translate the known minimum/small-volume `[k]`-trade classifications into a clean classification of smallest `Q_k`-indistinguishable Boolean pairs. Decide whether this is expository background or yields a useful new representation theorem.

## O7 — Positive structural classes beyond Chow/PTF

Find classes with provably small reconstruction threshold for reasons tied to the artifact representations, not merely because their real Fourier degree is small. A useful target is a class with compact representation and `kappa=o(n)` plus an efficient exact reconstruction algorithm from `Q_k` data.
